 ## Private Cache
 
-Cached JPEG data may occupy at most 12 GiB. Before admitting a completed sheet, evict enough existing sheets to remain within that bound. Temporary render output is kept separately and removed on completion or failure. Eviction never deletes source footage or changes job-ticket semantics.
+Cached JPEG data may occupy at most 12 GiB. Before admitting a completed sheet, evict enough existing entries to remain within that bound. Temporary render output is kept separately and removed on completion or failure. Eviction never deletes source footage or changes job-ticket semantics.
 
-The eviction policy is still open. Candidates are LRU, frequency-based eviction with aging, and 2Q. LRU has little bookkeeping and follows recent work quickly but is vulnerable to sequential scans. Aged frequency counts protect repeatedly popular clips but add counter maintenance and can lag a project switch. 2Q separates first-use entries from reused entries, resisting scans at the cost of extra queues and a queue-size parameter. None changes the external interface, queue concurrency, or disk budget.
+### Eviction Policy: 2Q
+
+The cache uses a **2Q eviction policy** with two queues:
+
+- **A1in (Amateur queue, first-use entries)** — new entries are inserted at the head. On a cache hit in A1in, the entry is promoted to Am (moved to the head of Am). When A1in exceeds its size limit, the tail entry is evicted.
+- **Am (Professional queue, reused entries)** — entries that have been accessed at least twice. On a cache hit in Am, the entry is moved to the head of Am (MRU within Am). When Am exceeds its size limit, the tail entry is evicted.
+
+The total cache capacity is 12 GiB of JPEG data. The queue split is **A1in = 25%, Am = 75%** of the capacity (3 GiB / 9 GiB). This split is a tunable parameter; the initial values favor protecting the comparison working set during long screenings.
+
+All replacement-policy metadata (queue membership, access timestamps, per-entry byte sizes) stays private to the preview worker. The external interface, queue concurrency (4 active jobs), and disk budget are unchanged.
+
+## Decisions & Alternatives
+
+| Decision | Chosen | Alternatives Considered | Rationale |
+|----------|--------|------------------------|-----------|
+| Eviction policy | 2Q (two-queue with A1in/Am split) | LRU; Frequency-based with aging | 2Q protects repeatedly accessed comparison sheets from eviction during long sequential screenings. LRU would evict the working set under a scan; frequency+aging adds counter maintenance and lag on project switches. The 25/75 split favors the professional queue where comparison sheets live. |
+
+## Open Questions & Future Decisions
+
+### Resolved
+
+1. ✅ Eviction policy selected as 2Q with 25/75 A1in/Am split.
+
+### Deferred
+
+1. Runtime tuning of the A1in/Am split based on observed workload.
+2. Whether to track per-entry render cost for admission decisions beyond size.
